 'A direct question can ask for a fact or explanation: τίς; “who?”, τί; “what?” or “why?” in context, ποῦ; “where?”, πότε; “when?”, and διὰ τί; “why?” The Greek question mark is the semicolon. A question can use present or future forms.',
 'Interrogative τίς, τί is accented, unlike indefinite τις, τι, “someone, something.” It declines: τίνος, “of whom?”; τίνι, “to whom?”; τίνα, “whom?”; plural τίνες, “who?” The interrogative’s case marks its role inside the question.',
